w people are forgetting how  they're exhausted he's exhausted -  Darlene comes in she's obviously using  drugs she's out of her mind  she believes she saw Angela Elliot knows  this is not possible so he doesn't  really want to deal with Darlene he's  seen the photos of Angela's dead body  and as viewers we get mr. robot coming  and talking to us which he doesn't  usually do he tells us that Elliot is  shutting us out he's basically shutting  everyone out and we can see that that  dynamic of Elliot being the voice of  reason that that has basically flipped  Elliot decides to go to garson's office  he's going to deliver a package that's  going to get him access to the Wi-Fi  there when they get there it's obviously  set up  it's a honeypot he doesn't figure this  out until it's too late as viewers we  get the idea a little bit faster because  it's obviously set up nobody's there  they're looking around it doesn't look  like anybody's ever really work  there mr. robot says in the hall as  they're approaching that this is the  quietest building in Manhattan  I like the quirkiness here the man at  the counter eating fruity pebbles we  have another character talking loud they  like facetiming someone on the phone a  different language that we can't  understand and after Elliot gets himself  caught we hear the guy at the counter  fire up don't worry be happy' on his  iPod in that place through the halls it  continues playing as Elliott is dragged  away by two men and he's kicking and  shouting as they go back out in New  Jersey we meet the new character Janice  at Dom's place her mom thinks she's  invited Janice over to possibly set her  up with DOM but we learned that Janice  is actually the one pulling the strings  here she comes off as nerdy and harmless  at dinner then does this 180 and reveals  her true colors when they're all alone  outside Janice tells Dom that she's  gonna have to wake up in the morning and  go do the interview about the Santiago  case because that